---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import ContactCTA from "../../components/ContactCTA.astro"
import Hero from "../../components/Hero.astro"
---
<BaseLayout title="November Events | Side Quests Colorado" description="November 2026 Events">
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper about">
			<Hero
				title="November 2026 Bike Events"
				tagline="Check out the cool events you can go to in November."
			>
				<img
					width="1553"
					height="873"
					src="/assets/novembercrafts.png"
					alt="A bike and daisies."
				/>
    </Hero>
	<section>
		<h2 class="section-title">More Events</h2>
						<p class="space-p">Remember to check each group or events particpation criteria or RSVP method before going. Some groups are only open to individuals who identify a certain way. Some require RSVPs. Respect their participation rules.</p>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 7 (14, 21, & 28): Arts and Cats</h3>
				<p class="space-p">Every Saturday between 2 PM and 5 PM, it’s Arts & Cats open crafting time. Bring a project you’re working on, or grab some supplies from our lockers. </p>
				<p>Learn more on the <a href="https://www.catpeopleden.com/calendar/arts-cats-11-07" target="_blank">Cat People Denver Event Page</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 7: Book Fair</h3>
				<p class="space-p">Grab a pint and pick up a book! On Saturday, November 7th from 1-4PM, join @redlegbrewco for a book fair on the Red Leg lawn! Come meet local authors, check out their books, and maybe even buy some of their products! This event is free to attend and will feature other local vendors.</p>
				<p>Learn more on the <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DfDP9uYFMmH/" target="_blank">@redlegbrewco post</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 7: Rocky Mountain Indigenous Dancers</h3>
				<p class="space-p">Experience the power and beauty of traditional indigenous dance, music and history that honors the rich cultural heritage of Native communities from the Rocky Mountain region. This family-friendly event offers an opportunity to learn about the significance of Native dances and regalia, and to connect with indigenous traditions through live performance.</p>
				<p>No RSVP required. Learn more on the<a href="https://events.anythinklibraries.org/event/17714910" target="_blank">Think Libraries website</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 7: Author Talk: Tending the Vines</h3>
				<p class="space-p">From 3 PM to 5 PM, join author Ashia S. Ajani to discuss Black ecological literature and her new book, Tending the Vines: Black Abundance in Eight Plants.</p>
				<p><a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/author-talk-tending-the-vines-tickets-2002311253861?utm_campaign=feed&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=later-linkinbio&keep_tld=true" target="_blank">RSVP on the EventBrite page</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 8: Learn to Crochet</h3>
				<p class="space-p">From 2 PM to 5 PM, learn how to crochet with Louisa! No experience necessary. If you’ve attended one of these before, she’ll build on the skills you learned last time. This class is great for all ages.</p>
				<p>Learn more on the <a href="https://www.catpeopleden.com/calendar/crochet-for-beginners-1-99sty" target="_blank">Cat People Denver Event Page</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 14: Dungeons and Dragons One-Shots</h3>
				<p class="space-p">6 PM to 9:30 PM at Fiction Beer</p>
				<p>Learn more and register on the <a href="https://dungeonsndrafts.com/quest-board" target="_blank">Dugeons and Drafts Website</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 15: Indigenous + Queer Open Mic Night</h3>
				<p class="space-p">5:30 PM to 8:00 PM at First People’s Community Center, 3745 E. Prospect Rd., Fort Collins, CO</p>
				<p>Learn more and register on the <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DfDgVqHzAjE/" target="_blank">@firstpeoplescommunitycenter IG Post</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 15: Drum Cirlce</h3>
				<p class="space-p">1 PM to 3 PM at Staunton State Park</p>
				<p>Learn more and register on the <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DfSYyxMAi08/" target="_blank">@stauntonstatepark IG Post</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 19: Rites of Passage Skate Night (for CSU students)</h3>
				<p class="space-p">8:45 PM to 10:45 PM at Rollerland (324 S Link Ln, Fort Collins, CO 80015)</p>
				<p>Learn more and RSVP on the <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DfBIJCFvITI/" target="_blank">@baacc_csu IG post</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 22: Sapphic Thirft </h3>
				<p class="space-p">11 aM to 1:15 PM at Cha's Cafe and Atlier 925 W 8th Ave, Denver, CO 80204</p>
				<p>Learn more and RSVP on the <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DfNNGyKTNdM/" target="_blank">@sapphicthrift IG post</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 29: An Indigenous Winter Artist Market</h3>
				<p class="space-p">10 AM to 5 PM at Dairy Arts Center in Boulder, CO</p>
				<p>Learn more on the <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DfYpt9Etatk/" target="_blank">@themoodyreaderbooks IG post</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<h3>Nov 29: Adult Book Fair</h3>
				<p class="space-p">12 PM to 4 PM at Pours and Provisions (3053 W 104th Ave, Westminster, CO 80031)</p>
				<p>Learn more on the <a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DfFlTZkmZvz/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&mdxt=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==" target="_blank">@themoodyreaderbooks IG post</a></p>
			</div>
	</section>
	<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Disclaimers</h2>
					<div class="content">
						<p>
							Colorado Side Quests does not endorse any of the events, organizations and individuals listed on this page or on our site. The information provided is information only. Attend any event at your own risk. Neither Colorado Side Quests, nor it's contributors are not responsible for your health, safety or wellbeing and will not be held responsible for any real or percieved injuries you face after attending any of the events listed on our site or by using any third-party links on our site. We cannot control you or any third-party individual or organization or their website. Use the Colorado Side Quests website or Instagram at your own risk.
						</p>
					</div>
			</section>
      </main>

		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.space-p{
		padding-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	h3 {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	img {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.section-title {
		grid-column-start: 1;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		grid-column: 2 / 4;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.about {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 60% 1fr;
		}

		.about > :global(:first-child) {
			grid-column-start: 2;
		}

		section {
			display: contents;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}
	}
</style>